  "transcript": {
    "text": "Drake once said, \"Relationships slowing me down. It's slowing down the vision. Guess I'm not in a position to deal with commitment.\" And sometimes that's the harsh truth that nobody wants to admit. Not every season in your life is meant for love, and sometimes you're building something that requires a selfish level of focus. Long nights and early mornings and missing plans and saying no more than you say yes. And when you know you can't give somebody the time, energy, and presence they deserve, forcing a relationship just because you're lonely usually ends up bad for everybody involved. But there's also nothing wrong with admitting that right now, the vision comes first, because the wrong relationship can make you feel guilty for becoming who you said you always wanted to be. Sometimes being alone isn't a lack of love, it's choosing not to sacrifice your future just to feel less lonely in the present.",
